00:46:06,090 --> 00:46:07,730
from the skill I just taught her.

819
00:46:07,730 --> 00:46:09,530
Data Dan is working on the Google Form.

820
00:46:09,530 --> 00:46:13,010
I can actually see him creating the form live for me.

821
00:46:13,010 --> 00:46:16,010
And then what's nice about this is once the form is created,

822
00:46:16,010 --> 00:46:18,890
I'm actually going to ask Data Dan to turn it into a QR code

823
00:46:18,890 --> 00:46:21,450
and have you all scan it and fill out those two questions.

824
00:46:21,450 --> 00:46:22,970
So on average, how many coffee cups

825
00:46:22,970 --> 00:46:25,290
do you drink a day and your favorite coffee shop

826
00:46:25,290 --> 00:46:26,450
in San Francisco?

827
00:46:26,450 --> 00:46:29,490
And then we'll take all of that data, give it to Sonya,

828
00:46:29,490 --> 00:46:33,030
and then have email Ethan kind of consolidate all that analysis

829
00:46:33,030 --> 00:46:36,090
and send it out to, let's see who the top coffee shop owner

830
00:46:36,090 --> 00:46:36,970
is.

831
00:46:36,970 --> 00:46:39,150
And this is kind of a good way to see

832
00:46:39,150 --> 00:46:42,730
how you can take a very simple task that usually

833
00:46:42,770 --> 00:46:43,570
takes a lot of time.

834
00:46:43,570 --> 00:46:46,250
For example, an event planner at a company

835
00:46:46,250 --> 00:46:49,250
who needs to handle dietary restrictions for a 10,000

836
00:46:49,250 --> 00:46:51,690
person on site, or a user researcher that

837
00:46:51,690 --> 00:46:54,330
wants to collect data from all of their different customers

838
00:46:54,330 --> 00:46:56,650
who are using Grokbot or any other tool,

839
00:46:56,650 --> 00:47:00,130
how you can basically do all of these tools within Grokbot

840
00:47:00,130 --> 00:47:03,850
and then have it kind of orchestrate that work for me.

841
00:47:03,850 --> 00:47:07,770
I'm going to go ahead and set this one more time.

842
00:47:07,770 --> 00:47:09,650
While this is working, let me actually show you

843
00:47:09,650 --> 00:47:12,930
the approval situation since we are seeing it here.

844
00:47:12,930 --> 00:47:16,330
You'll notice that in the settings, when you actually

845
00:47:16,330 --> 00:47:19,810
scroll down here, you will see a particular set of rules

846
00:47:19,810 --> 00:47:23,110
that you can allow Grokbot to basically do with or without

847
00:47:23,110 --> 00:47:24,330
your permission.

848
00:47:24,330 --> 00:47:27,410
So what I'll actually show it is I'll say something like, hey,

849
00:47:27,410 --> 00:47:29,390
I don't want you to reply emails for me

850
00:47:29,390 --> 00:47:32,930
unless you explicitly ask for my permission first.

851
00:47:32,930 --> 00:47:36,030
Or similarly, I want you to be able to create slides for me

852
00:47:36,030 --> 00:47:39,050
automatically without asking for my permission.

853
00:47:39,050 --> 00:47:41,610
And so that makes it a lot easier for you

854
00:47:41,610 --> 00:47:45,650
to kind of granularly control what Grokbot can or cannot do,

855
00:47:45,650 --> 00:47:48,610
especially when it's doing long running tasks that you

856
00:47:48,610 --> 00:47:52,010
want to be a little bit aware of or kind of cognizant

857
00:47:52,010 --> 00:47:54,820
of what it's doing.

858
00:47:54,820 --> 00:47:59,640
Give this a little more time while it's working.

859
00:47:59,640 --> 00:48:01,700
One thing that I do want to say about Grokbot

860
00:48:01,700 --> 00:48:04,500
and how basically it's able to run

861
00:48:04,500 --> 00:48:06,340
is that the computers that it's using on

862
00:48:06,340 --> 00:48:09,380
are all isolated, meaning that one Grokbot cannot access

863
00:48:09,380 --> 00:48:11,020
another Grokbot's computer.

864
00:48:11,020 --> 00:48:14,220
So the fact that Grokbot is working on this Google form

865
00:48:14,220 --> 00:48:16,300
here is not going to impact the fact

866
00:48:16,300 --> 00:48:19,460
that SlideSonia is working on the slides over here.

867
00:48:19,460 --> 00:48:21,700
And that makes it easy, actually, for one Grokbot

868
00:48:21,700 --> 00:48:24,060
to talk to another and work on two different things

869
00:48:24,060 --> 00:48:25,340
at the same time.

870
00:48:25,340 --> 00:48:27,780
So a way that I use this is I often

871
00:48:27,780 --> 00:48:31,220
edit the same set of slides that my Grokbot is editing.

872
00:48:31,220 --> 00:48:34,100
And that makes it really easy because I can have SlideSonia

873
00:48:34,100 --> 00:48:37,060
edit slide one or two of mine on my slides,

874
00:48:37,060 --> 00:48:39,420
and I can edit the 10th or 11th slide.

875
00:48:39,420 --> 00:48:42,420
And we're not actually conflicting or making changes.

876
00:48:42,420 --> 00:48:46,180
We're both kind of collaborating on the same set of tasks.

877
00:48:46,180 --> 00:48:47,620
And that's kind of, at the end of the day,

878
00:48:47,620 --> 00:48:48,540
what Grokbot is.

879
00:48:48,540 --> 00:48:51,380
It's a colleague that you can collaborate on.

880
00:48:51,380 --> 00:48:55,300
What's nice about SlideSonia is in her description here,

881
00:48:55,300 --> 00:48:57,820
you can see that I've given her very explicit instructions

882
00:48:57,820 --> 00:49:00,340
on how to edit an existing slide deck.

883
00:49:00,340 --> 00:49:02,260
I can tell her that you're supposed to be using

884
00:49:02,260 --> 00:49:05,460
a particular font with particular colors.

885
00:49:05,460 --> 00:49:08,620
I actually always ask her to take a screenshot of the slide

886
00:49:08,620 --> 00:49:11,380
that she's created once she's done and send it back to me.

887
00:49:11,380 --> 00:49:13,300
And this kind of makes it a lot easier for me

888
00:49:13,300 --> 00:49:14,940
to go back and forth with SlideSonia

889
00:49:14,940 --> 00:49:17,780
because she already has this predefined set of notions

