5096
04:37:47,600 --> 04:37:51,030
they can be extra capable of.

5097
04:37:51,030 --> 04:37:55,630
Another thing is we can possibly think one level further

5098
04:37:55,630 --> 04:37:58,110
rather than just fix the thing.

5099
04:37:58,110 --> 04:38:02,590
This also could be known as reduced repetition,

5100
04:38:02,590 --> 04:38:08,230
that sometimes I repeat a prompt to my agents too often,

5101
04:38:08,230 --> 04:38:11,590
that it's a waste of my time if I have to type in or copy

5102
04:38:11,590 --> 04:38:14,910
paste the same thing and send it to the agent 10 times.

5103
04:38:14,910 --> 04:38:17,150
You can think it one level further

5104
04:38:17,150 --> 04:38:20,630
about what actually needs to be done

5105
04:38:20,630 --> 04:38:24,550
and then extract it into some layer, either via a playbook

5106
04:38:24,550 --> 04:38:28,550
or via some other bots to nudge another bot for you

5107
04:38:28,550 --> 04:38:30,810
at the right time.

5108
04:38:30,810 --> 04:38:34,010
The last thing I think is also very important for using

5109
04:38:34,010 --> 04:38:35,890
engineering with Cursor Cloud agents

5110
04:38:35,890 --> 04:38:38,350
is to have a complete feedback loop.

5111
04:38:38,350 --> 04:38:41,670
No matter what type of engineering tasks you have,

5112
04:38:41,670 --> 04:38:43,910
it needs to have a feedback loop in order for an agent

5113
04:38:43,910 --> 04:38:47,150
to understand a signal of success versus failure.

5114
04:38:47,150 --> 04:38:48,790
That's also very helpful for a group bot

5115
04:38:48,790 --> 04:38:51,710
to determine whether they should nudge further

5116
04:38:51,710 --> 04:38:56,230
or whether they should stop and let it merge.

5117
04:38:56,230 --> 04:38:58,110
For example, you can let your agent

5118
04:38:58,110 --> 04:39:00,830
