06:19:10,250 --> 06:19:11,090
That's a good idea.

6967
06:19:11,090 --> 06:19:11,610
Yeah, yeah.

6968
06:19:11,610 --> 06:19:17,810
So we should probably get some design for each of our P0s.

6969
06:19:17,810 --> 06:19:18,290
Cool.

6970
06:19:18,290 --> 06:19:18,770
All right.

6971
06:19:18,770 --> 06:19:21,750
So let's send that off.

6972
06:19:21,750 --> 06:19:27,550
And while that cooks, we'll pull up the virtual machine, which

6973
06:19:27,550 --> 06:19:29,390
Grokbot has access to.

6974
06:19:29,390 --> 06:19:33,470
And as we talked about, these are colleagues with a computer.

6975
06:19:33,470 --> 06:19:36,710
And so it is very helpful to give these agents,

6976
06:19:36,710 --> 06:19:39,990
these colleagues, give Grokbot its own virtual machine,

6977
06:19:39,990 --> 06:19:43,990
its own computer in the cloud, where it can actually do work.

6978
06:19:43,990 --> 06:19:45,790
It can navigate the web.

6979
06:19:45,790 --> 06:19:49,190
You can log in, and it can use your credentials

6980
06:19:49,190 --> 06:19:53,590
across various services to actually get work done.

6981
06:19:53,590 --> 06:19:57,020
And you can see up here top right,

6982
06:19:57,020 --> 06:19:58,500
you can see Teach It a Task.

6983
06:19:58,500 --> 06:20:03,100
And so you can actually record your workflows directly

6984
06:20:03,100 --> 06:20:04,460
on this machine.

6985
06:20:04,460 --> 06:20:07,220
And Agent can watch and learn and be

6986
06:20:07,220 --> 06:20:10,420
able to replicate and reproduce the work that you are doing.

6987
06:20:10,500 --> 06:20:14,420
So we often hear our sales team, our go-to-market team,

6988
06:20:14,420 --> 06:20:17,660
have these very complex Salesforce workflows,

6989
06:20:17,660 --> 06:20:19,740
these complex processes that need

6990
06:20:19,740 --> 06:20:21,220
to be replicated again and again.

6991
06:20:21,220 --> 06:20:24,460
And it's very helpful to be able to teach an agent with more

6992
06:20:24,460 --> 06:20:26,740
than just words or more than just spoken word

6993
06:20:26,740 --> 06:20:30,260
to actually be able to record the work that you are doing.

6994
06:20:30,260 --> 06:20:33,940
And the agent actually, every time it uses one of those tasks

6995
06:20:33,940 --> 06:20:35,900
or goes through one of those tasks,

6996
06:20:35,900 --> 06:20:37,700
also has the ability to refine that skill

6997
06:20:37,700 --> 06:20:39,300
and, again, follow that feedback mechanism

6998
06:20:39,300 --> 06:20:40,380
that we talked about earlier.

6999
06:20:40,740 --> 06:20:42,340
Really, if you're working in bespoke systems

7000
06:20:42,340 --> 06:20:46,010
or custom systems, I think that's really invaluable.

7001
06:20:46,010 --> 06:20:46,850
Okay, very cool.

7002
06:20:46,850 --> 06:20:49,770
So it looks like we have two separate handoffs,

7003
06:20:49,770 --> 06:20:53,290
one to engineering manager Emily

7004
06:20:53,290 --> 06:20:57,290
to actually start going on some prototypes for the spec.

7005
06:20:57,290 --> 06:21:00,450
And then the other is over to Pixel

7006
06:21:00,450 --> 06:21:04,410
to actually start working on some designs and some mocks.

7007
06:21:04,410 --> 06:21:05,850
Yeah, and I think what's cool

7008
06:21:05,850 --> 06:21:08,330
about the design workflow here is Pixel,

7009
06:21:08,330 --> 06:21:10,930
I mentioned earlier, is trained on just how

7010
06:21:11,570 --> 06:21:13,770
to be a great AI designer, but also it has context

