06:21:16,210 --> 06:21:18,210
And so in this case, we use Figma,

7013
06:21:18,210 --> 06:21:20,330
and so the design system lives in Figma,

7014
06:21:20,330 --> 06:21:23,930
but Pixel also sort of has reference files in its context

7015
06:21:23,930 --> 06:21:26,330
that sort of teach it how to design for our airline.

7016
06:21:26,330 --> 06:21:28,890
And so what this does is it makes it so that

7017
06:21:28,890 --> 06:21:30,770
we're not starting from scratch every time.

7018
06:21:30,770 --> 06:21:33,090
The agent has a ton of embedded context

7019
06:21:33,090 --> 06:21:36,010
on our preferred fonts and colors, UI patterns,

7020
06:21:37,370 --> 06:21:39,410
no-nos, we thought it over time, for example,

7021
06:21:39,410 --> 06:21:41,490
like never make X buttons on the left corner

7022
06:21:41,490 --> 06:21:42,610
and things like this.

7023
06:21:42,610 --> 06:21:44,730
And that really kind of gives this designer

7024
06:21:44,730 --> 06:21:47,050
the ability to iterate really, really quickly

7025
06:21:47,050 --> 06:21:49,650
and then get things mostly right on the first try

7026
06:21:49,650 --> 06:21:51,450
versus having to start from scratch every time.

7027
06:21:51,450 --> 06:21:53,810
And it looks like we got some designs.

7028
06:21:53,810 --> 06:21:56,960
What do we think?

7029
06:21:56,960 --> 06:21:58,560
Those are some expensive tickets.

7030
06:21:59,920 --> 06:22:01,720
It looks like we have two different options,

7031
06:22:01,720 --> 06:22:05,880
option A and option B, which Pixel has designed.

