I encourage them, like I said, they

9204
07:51:53,620 --> 07:51:56,640
learn to loop in the other bots as needed.

9205
07:51:56,640 --> 07:51:58,360
And this bot might seem like a small one

9206
07:51:58,360 --> 07:51:59,680
because it's very simple.

9207
07:51:59,680 --> 07:52:01,280
But it's so important, especially

9208
07:52:01,280 --> 07:52:04,240
if you're trying to do any sort of outbound or move quickly

9209
07:52:04,240 --> 07:52:05,440
on communications.

9210
07:52:05,440 --> 07:52:07,700
It's nice to have a bot you can just trust to do this

9211
07:52:07,700 --> 07:52:08,520
stuff.

9212
07:52:08,520 --> 07:52:09,800
Obviously, you have some emails

9213
07:52:09,800 --> 07:52:11,000
that are really sensitive.

9214
07:52:11,000 --> 07:52:13,320
So you might ask it to just keep them as drafts rather than

9215
07:52:13,320 --> 07:52:14,640
just sending them right away.

9216
07:52:14,640 --> 07:52:16,680
But even then, it will learn from the delta

9217
07:52:16,680 --> 07:52:20,100
between the draft it created and what was actually sent

9218
07:52:20,100 --> 07:52:22,020
and get better and better over time, with the end vision

9219
07:52:22,020 --> 07:52:24,740
being that you don't need to think about it at all.

9220
07:52:24,740 --> 07:52:28,180
OK, final tip, I have a miscellaneous bot.

9221
07:52:28,180 --> 07:52:30,340
And this bot has one job, which is basically

9222
07:52:30,340 --> 07:52:33,620
to be kind of a trash can for all of the random requests

9223
07:52:33,620 --> 07:52:34,420
I have.

9224
07:52:34,420 --> 07:52:36,900
Today, I wanted to see if Drake's album dropped.

9225
07:52:36,900 --> 07:52:38,220
It is not yet, sadly.

9226
07:52:38,220 --> 07:52:39,900
But what's really cool about this one

9227
07:52:39,900 --> 07:52:41,780
is I can just ask it random things

9228
07:52:41,780 --> 07:52:44,140
without polluting the context of the other bots.

9229
07:52:44,140 --> 07:52:46,100
And if it ever has any important tasks

9230
07:52:46,100 --> 07:52:48,400
to do where it needs to transfer that context,

9231
07:52:48,400 --> 07:52:51,280
I can just ask and say, hey, you learned about XYZ.

9232
07:52:51,280 --> 07:52:53,580
Go tell ProdBot about what you've

9233
07:52:53,580 --> 07:52:56,100
learned so that it can get better in the future.

9234
07:52:56,100 --> 07:52:57,780
Sadly, Drake's album isn't out.

9235
07:52:57,780 --> 07:52:58,760
It checked Instagram.

9236
07:52:58,760 --> 07:53:00,280
But who knows?

9237
07:53:00,280 --> 07:53:02,060
We'll get there maybe later tonight.

9238
07:53:02,060 --> 07:53:03,940
OK, those were all my bots.

9239
07:53:03,940 --> 07:53:07,040
I think ProdBot is still going.

9240
07:53:07,040 --> 07:53:08,800
It's kicking off a cloud agent.

9241
07:53:08,800 --> 07:53:10,720
And hopefully, it finishes sometime soon.

9242
07:53:10,720 --> 07:53:13,480
But you'll notice, because it has access to GrokBot,

9243
07:53:13,480 --> 07:53:16,920
it can actually just take a look at the interface

9244
07:53:16,920 --> 07:53:18,780
without needing to go find it anywhere.

9245
07:53:18,780 --> 07:53:20,960
And it can drive it and QA it.

9246
07:53:20,960 --> 07:53:23,980
And as these tests happen, it's very easily verifiable,

9247
07:53:23,980 --> 07:53:26,820
whether it's shipped the right thing or not.

9248
07:53:26,820 --> 07:53:29,580
And so I think all of these bots are very powerful.

9249
07:53:29,580 --> 07:53:32,220
And most importantly, they're all powerful in conjunction.

9250
07:53:32,220 --> 07:53:34,820
So when CloseBot gets some feedback,

9251
07:53:34,820 --> 07:53:36,700
it can pass it to ProdBot.

9252
07:53:36,700 --> 07:53:40,100
Or when ProdBot is trying to get across some of the key product

9253
07:53:40,100 --> 07:53:42,820
decisions that we've made, it can pass that context

9254
07:53:42,820 --> 07:53:45,700
off to CloseBot so that it can sell the right stuff.

9255
07:53:45,700 --> 07:53:48,620
And overall, I think the key framework that you folks

9256
07:53:48,620 --> 07:53:50,680
need to keep in mind is you want

9257
07:53:50,680 --> 07:53:53,920
to start to try and productize yourself as much as possible

9258
07:53:53,920 --> 07:53:57,040
and give away all of your LEGOs, no matter how delightful they

9259
07:53:57,040 --> 07:53:59,720
are, so that you can focus on the highest leverage thing.

9260
07:53:59,720 --> 07:54:02,280
Because that is what helps you win in a world where everyone

9261
07:54:02,280 --> 07:54:05,920
is shipping just as fast, if not faster for now.

9262
07:54:05,920 --> 07:54:07,560
So keep all that in mind.

9263
07:54:07,560 --> 07:54:08,400
But those are my bots.

9264
07:54:08,400 --> 07:54:11,360
Let's go back to the presentation.

9265
07:54:11,360 --> 07:54:14,290
OK, some final pieces.

9266
07:54:14,290 --> 07:54:17,010
What we learned, let your bots run free.

9267
07:54:17,010 --> 07:54:18,350
I am going to say this forever.

9268
07:54:18,450 --> 07:54:20,770
Give them access to as much as you are possibly

9269
07:54:20,770 --> 07:54:22,970
comfortable with, because that is the only way they

9270
07:54:22,970 --> 07:54:25,390
will be able to do work end to end.

9271
07:54:25,390 --> 07:54:26,510
You want to invest in them.

9272
07:54:26,510 --> 07:54:29,830
So you might find times where you need to course correct

9273
07:54:29,830 --> 07:54:30,310
a bot.

9274
07:54:30,310 --> 07:54:32,970
And with an agent, you might have the instinct of, man,

9275
07:54:32,970 --> 07:54:35,270
I spent too many tokens on course correcting it.

9276
07:54:35,270 --> 07:54:36,710
The context is polluted.

9277
07:54:36,710 --> 07:54:38,630
Let me just get rid of it and start a new one.

9278
07:54:38,630 --> 07:54:40,510
In this case, your key advantage is

9279
07:54:40,510 --> 07:54:41,790
that your bots get really good

9280
07:54:41,790 --> 07:54:43,230
as you spend more time with them.

9281
07:54:43,230 --> 07:54:46,710
And obviously, as the team has learned internally,

9282
07:54:46,710 --> 07:54:48,730
the more time you spend, the better you do.

9283
07:54:48,730 --> 07:54:50,730
And so it's really important to really believe

9284
07:54:50,730 --> 07:54:53,410
in your bots the same way you would with employees.

9285
07:54:53,410 --> 07:54:55,290
And the other piece to keep in mind here

9286
07:54:55,290 --> 07:54:56,930
is the other way to invest in them

9287
07:54:56,930 --> 07:54:59,330
is by giving them really good skills and tools.

9288
07:54:59,330 --> 07:55:02,570
So it's very easy to say, hey, make this cooler.

9289
07:55:02,570 --> 07:55:04,290
And that could be your prompt that you

9290
07:55:04,290 --> 07:55:05,770
want your bot to execute on.

9291
07:55:05,770 --> 07:55:08,210
But obviously, it's not going to do a great job.

9292
07:55:08,210 --> 07:55:10,170
And it's going to probably get stuck somewhere

9293
07:55:10,170 --> 07:55:11,570
and ask you a few questions.

9294
07:55:11,570 --> 07:55:14,210
The more intentionality you put behind that task

9295
07:55:14,210 --> 07:55:16,650
in the first place lets you repeat it over and over again

9296
07:55:17,590 --> 07:55:18,950
without that many hitches.

9297
07:55:18,950 --> 07:55:22,990
And then finally, it is worth you taking one to two hours

9298
07:55:22,990 --> 07:55:25,520
and just thinking about your day.

9299
07:55:25,520 --> 07:55:26,640
I know that sounds dumb.

9300
07:55:26,640 --> 07:55:28,240
I know you're like, I need to move quickly.

9301
07:55:28,240 --> 07:55:30,520
But it is so, so important to just take the time.

9302
07:55:30,520 --> 07:55:31,600
I don't care when.

9303
07:55:31,600 --> 07:55:35,560
Just do it and figure out what you want to delegate.

9304
07:55:35,560 --> 07:55:39,040
Because doing that intentionally will save you so many hours

9305
07:55:39,040 --> 07:55:41,360
versus just spinning up bots and hoping they do things

9306
07:55:41,360 --> 07:55:43,520
for you without having a true intent

9307
07:55:43,520 --> 07:55:45,460
around what they should do.

9308
07:55:46,290 --> 07:55:48,690
Now, I have a bonus round with some tips and tricks.

9309
07:55:48,690 --> 07:55:50,970
I was watching the livestream earlier.

9310
07:55:50,970 --> 07:55:52,970
And some people were like, this is expensive,

9311
07:55:52,970 --> 07:55:55,710
which is true in some ways, not true in others.

9312
07:55:55,710 --> 07:55:57,490
And we're working on it.

9313
07:55:57,490 --> 07:56:00,130
But there are some really easy, high-leverage tips

9314
07:56:00,130 --> 07:56:01,970
that can make your life a lot easier.

9315
07:56:01,970 --> 07:56:05,290
The first is that browser use is super powerful.

9316
07:56:05,290 --> 07:56:08,970
And it unblocks your bot from doing a lot of things

9317
07:56:08,970 --> 07:56:10,450
that it couldn't do if it didn't have

9318
07:56:10,450 --> 07:56:12,810
MCPs or APIs or some other connection.

9319
07:56:12,830 --> 07:56:15,810
But it's also expensive to run multiple times.

9320
07:56:15,810 --> 07:56:18,950
And the easiest way to solve for this

9321
07:56:18,950 --> 07:56:23,010
is to bias towards using APIs and using interfaces

9322
07:56:23,010 --> 07:56:26,510
that people have already built, or to actually kind of hack

9323
07:56:26,510 --> 07:56:27,710
it a little bit.

9324
07:56:27,710 --> 07:56:30,630
You can ask your bot to look at network requests

9325
07:56:30,630 --> 07:56:33,450
while it does a task once, and then figure out

9326
07:56:33,450 --> 07:56:37,110
which APIs are being hit while it's doing that task,

9327
07:56:37,110 --> 07:56:40,750
and then go and start to just hit those directly, which

9328
07:56:40,750 --> 07:56:42,710
takes way less time, first of all.

9329
07:56:42,710 --> 07:56:44,130
And it's also way more token efficient,

9330
07:56:44,130 --> 07:56:46,930
because you are no longer needing to go through the browser

9331
07:56:46,930 --> 07:56:47,450
interface.

9332
07:56:47,450 --> 07:56:48,930
And you can just do it all directly.

9333
07:56:48,930 --> 07:56:50,150
So ask your bot.

9334
07:56:50,150 --> 07:56:52,250
And this is true for all optimizations, by the way,

9335
07:56:52,250 --> 07:56:54,650
that you guys have probably been thinking of or taking notes

9336
07:56:54,650 --> 07:56:55,130
on.

9337
07:56:55,130 --> 07:56:56,770
Always just ask your bot how to do it,

9338
07:56:56,770 --> 07:56:59,810
because it will figure it out for you, which is very nice.

9339
07:56:59,810 --> 07:57:03,460
But be wary of browser use more than once.

9340
07:57:03,460 --> 07:57:05,500
And if you can get around it and scale quickly,

9341
07:57:05,500 --> 07:57:07,410
you absolutely should.

9342
07:57:07,410 --> 07:57:09,450
Second piece, routines.

9343
07:57:09,450 --> 07:57:11,090
When I was looking through some of the data

9344
07:57:11,090 --> 07:57:14,190
around the frequency of routines that people set,

9345
07:57:14,190 --> 07:57:15,590
I was a little shocked.

9346
07:57:15,590 --> 07:57:18,950
And it freaks me out how often you guys are running things.

9347
07:57:18,950 --> 07:57:21,230
But I think the most important part about routines

9348
07:57:21,230 --> 07:57:22,030
is to audit them.

9349
07:57:22,030 --> 07:57:23,690
And you don't have to do this yourself.

9350
07:57:23,690 --> 07:57:25,590
Again, get a bot to do it for you.

9351
07:57:25,590 --> 07:57:29,910
But the most important piece is be very intentional about how

9352
07:57:29,910 --> 07:57:31,190
often your routines are running.

9353
07:57:31,190 --> 07:57:33,050
They're really powerful, but most people

9354
07:57:33,050 --> 07:57:35,630
over-index on how often they need to be running.

9355
07:57:35,630 --> 07:57:37,550
And they think, this routine is so important.

9356
07:57:37,550 --> 07:57:39,510
I need to run it every 15 minutes, which comes out

9357
07:57:39,510 --> 07:57:40,990
to 100 times a day.

9358
07:57:40,990 --> 07:57:43,050
So that is a very expensive routine.

9359
07:57:43,050 --> 07:57:45,850
See if you can be a little more nifty with them.

9360
07:57:45,850 --> 07:57:47,830
So it's not just running them fewer times.

9361
07:57:47,830 --> 07:57:50,610
If you really need a routine, try and run them on webhooks.

9362
07:57:50,610 --> 07:57:53,330
Or try and run them with some sort of inbound signal

9363
07:57:53,330 --> 07:57:56,290
that will let your bots actually take in an input

9364
07:57:56,290 --> 07:57:58,330
and then run it, rather than just having it blindly

9365
07:57:58,330 --> 07:57:59,890
run on a schedule.

9366
07:57:59,890 --> 07:58:01,730
So those two things alone will probably

9367
07:58:01,730 --> 07:58:03,210
save you a bunch in tokens.

9368
07:58:03,210 --> 07:58:04,730
I know there was some demand for that.

9369
07:58:04,730 --> 07:58:09,190
OK, even more final tips before they came me off stage.

9370
07:58:09,190 --> 07:58:10,090
Make a voice bot.

9371
07:58:10,090 --> 07:58:12,190
Obviously, I love mine.

9372
07:58:12,190 --> 07:58:13,690
Please do this for yourself.

9373
07:58:13,690 --> 07:58:17,870
It is the most underrated way to get words out to other people.

9374
07:58:17,870 --> 07:58:20,550
It's have a bot that copies your voice.

9375
07:58:20,550 --> 07:58:21,630
Import your cookies.

9376
07:58:21,630 --> 07:58:24,130
This lets you stay signed in across a lot of different tools.

9377
07:58:24,130 --> 07:58:27,110
And it also stops you from having

9378
07:58:27,110 --> 07:58:30,950
to constantly take over the bot's computer and help out.

9379
07:58:30,950 --> 07:58:32,230
Group bots by expertise.

9380
07:58:32,230 --> 07:58:34,150
This is kind of a personal preference thing,

9381
07:58:34,150 --> 07:58:37,670
but I love having my bots grouped by what they do.

9382
07:58:37,670 --> 07:58:40,370
And so if a bot is really good at just handling a customer,

9383
07:58:40,370 --> 07:58:42,890
I will give it everything customer related.

9384
07:58:42,890 --> 07:58:46,210
And if a bot is really good at data analysis,

9385
07:58:46,210 --> 07:58:47,390
that will be its sole job.

9386
07:58:47,390 --> 07:58:49,970
Because sometimes there are weird compounding pieces

9387
07:58:49,970 --> 07:58:52,090
that happen that we don't even know about.

9388
07:58:52,090 --> 07:58:53,990
And so when you're giving it to what

9389
07:58:53,990 --> 07:58:56,090
feel like completely different tasks,

9390
07:58:56,090 --> 07:58:58,170
you can still get some of the compounding benefits

9391
07:58:58,170 --> 07:59:01,210
as long as they all fall under the same expertise.

9392
07:59:01,210 --> 07:59:03,130
There are a few more on here, like Great Skills,

9393
07:59:03,130 --> 07:59:05,570
which we talked about how bots can learn from you.

9394
07:59:05,570 --> 07:59:07,670
And then auto optimization routines.

9395
07:59:07,670 --> 07:59:09,990
But I think the last one is also pretty important.

9396
07:59:09,990 --> 07:59:13,870
Having a bot that just exists to optimize your other bots,

9397
07:59:13,870 --> 07:59:15,910
that means better routines, figuring out

9398
07:59:15,910 --> 07:59:18,290
where they went wrong or where you had to ask multiple times

9399
07:59:18,290 --> 07:59:20,830
for something, and then making sure that doesn't happen again.

9400
07:59:20,830 --> 07:59:24,050
And overseeing how the other ones work and improving them

9401
07:59:24,050 --> 07:59:26,990
is way easier than having to do a lot of this yourself.

9402
07:59:26,990 --> 07:59:28,470
So save yourself the time.

9403
07:59:28,470 --> 07:59:31,010
You set it once, and then you forget it, which is really nice.

9404
07:59:31,010 --> 07:59:34,540
And I don't see enough people doing that.

9405
07:59:34,540 --> 07:59:35,380
OK.

9406
07:59:35,380 --> 07:59:40,680
So that is close to the end of what we've been doing here.

9407
07:59:40,680 --> 07:59:42,920
Thank you for your time and attention.

9408
07:59:42,920 --> 07:59:45,560
I am going to leave a QR code for Stockbot.

9409
07:59:45,560 --> 07:59:47,480
If you guys want to steal it, it's a fun one.

9410
07:59:47,480 --> 07:59:48,820
You should try and use it on us.

9411
07:59:48,820 --> 07:59:49,820
I think that would be cool.

9412
07:59:49,820 --> 07:59:51,680
I want to see what people come up with.

9413
07:59:51,680 --> 07:59:54,800
But I really appreciate everyone being around.

9414
07:59:54,800 --> 07:59:59,120
I think one of the coolest parts about these bots

9415
07:59:59,120 --> 08:00:00,280
and where they're headed.

9416
08:00:00,000 --> 08:00:10,540
Is just how creative you can be. The amount of different bots and different combinations of bots that I've seen has really blown me away.

9417
08:00:10,540 --> 08:00:15,660
And I think founders are the perfect group to figure out the edges of this entire thing.

9418
08:00:15,660 --> 08:00:22,460
I don't think we've hit the limits yet. And as we get closer and closer to figuring out what these bots can actually do and what they can't,

9419
08:00:22,460 --> 08:00:26,460
we're going to be looking for signal from you guys. So really appreciate it.

9420
08:00:26,540 --> 08:00:34,180
If you are on the livestream, we're going to send you back to Matt, Lauren, and Roshan to go and continue cooking.

9421
08:00:34,180 --> 08:00:47,740
So appreciate it. Thanks. OK. For those of you here, we will take 15 minutes and answer some questions you have.

9422
08:00:47,740 --> 08:00:52,460
So we'll have some facilitators who maybe have mics, if not, just yell really loudly and we'll go from there.

9423
08:00:52,460 --> 08:01:00,890
So raise your hand if you have a question and we'll get after it. Yes, up here.

9424
08:01:00,890 --> 08:01:06,810
The idea of treating bots like humans. So you said you should spend one to two hours setting bots up.

9425
08:01:06,810 --> 08:01:10,250
Do you have a framework or suggestions as to how you actually do this?

9426
08:01:10,250 --> 08:01:16,910
What's the way in which you create jobs or roles and responsibilities for bots?

9427
08:01:16,910 --> 08:01:20,950
Yeah, the question is, like, what's the best way to set them up essentially? Right.

9428
08:01:20,950 --> 08:01:24,310
I think when you're trying to be intentional, there are two things that matter. Right.

9429
08:01:24,310 --> 08:01:30,830
One is figuring out what you need them for. So like actually inventorying every single thing that you need to do is pretty important,

9430
08:01:30,830 --> 08:01:36,030
because then you can start to group those things. And like I said, I like my bots to be experts.

9431
08:01:36,030 --> 08:01:39,350
And so they will have a very specific domain that they're good at.

9432
08:01:39,350 --> 08:01:43,630
And then they will expand their scope as I have more questions for them outside of that domain.

9433
08:01:43,630 --> 08:01:46,910
And so I trust them to do things outside of what they've been assigned.

9434
08:01:46,910 --> 08:01:55,470
But for the most part, I try to group them in, you know, your finance bot or your job is dealing with customers or job is like marketing generally.

9435
08:01:55,470 --> 08:01:59,470
And that's worked for me. Some people really like having the chief of staff

9436
08:01:59,550 --> 08:02:04,670
bot that manages the others. I personally am not a fan, but it really comes down to personal preference.

9437
08:02:04,670 --> 08:02:09,550
Right. If you're someone who just wants all of the work abstracted away, you just want to talk to one.

9438
08:02:09,550 --> 08:02:15,110
It's a good way to go. But if you really like being a little control freak and getting into the weeds,

9439
08:02:15,110 --> 08:02:21,070
I think having multiple bots that are all experts that you can then train up is it's kind of a good way to go.

9440
08:02:21,070 --> 08:02:27,420
And I would love to give them little XP bars for something as you go. But, you know, we'll see. Yes. Right here.

9441
08:02:27,420 --> 08:02:33,020
I just I just had a question about managing robots on multiple computers.

9442
08:02:33,020 --> 08:02:37,900
Is there any tips for that to work kind of and not get confused in the whole ecosystem?

